  "strategy": "We'll optimize the sequence representation by dynamically adjusting the length to find better solutions. The core idea is to start from the parent sequence (if provided) and explore lengths around it, while systematicallyevolving the sequence through a combination of linear programming (LP) andgradient-based updates to minimize the AC1 bound.\n\nApproach and Rationale\nOur method addresses the optimization of the AC1 upper bound by leveraging sparsity in the problem structure and iteratively improving the sequence. The key elements are:\n- Dynamic sequence length adjustment (initialized to 96 but expands to 128/256 for better optimization)\n- Dual-phase optimization: LP-based improvement followed by gradient descent refinement\n- Penalized deviation from the parent sequence to ensure exploration\n- Early termination triggers based on improvement rate and stability\n\nThis approach directly targets the AC1 bound minimization without normalization, preserving problem invariance in scaling. The LP-based method enforces baruations implicitly through dual variables, while gradient descent provides directional refinement.\n\nMathematicial Specification\nWe consider a sequence $x = (x_1, ..., x_n)$ with $n$ variables. \n\n**Objective:** \nMinimize $\\\\min_{\\\\mathbf{x}} \\\\frac{2n \\\\cdot \\\\|\\\\mathbf{x}\\\\star\\\\mathbf{x}\\\\|_\\\\infty}{(\\\\sum_i x_i)^2}$\n\n**Variables:**\n- Continuous real numbers $x_i >=0$\n\n**Representation:**\n- Sequences are defined by their length $n$\n- Initialization: Use provided parent sequence or generate suitable defaults\n\n**LP Phase Formulation:**\n- Decision variables: Dual sequence $\\lambda$ (length $n$)\n- Constraints: Linear inequalities from the autocorrelation bound\n- Objective: Maximize dual sum while maintaining autocorrelation controls\n- Chiion: Convert solutions and gradients to scaled adjustments\n\n**Gradient Phase Formulation:**\n- Computes the gradient of the AC1 bound\n- Projects complementary slackness conditions for improvement\n- Mixes sequences through positive scaling balances\n\nImplementation Procedure\n1. **Initialization:**\n   - Load parent sequence if provided\n   - Default initialization: Dirichlet distribution with shape parameter $\\\\alpha=1.7$\n\n2. **Phase Setup:**\n   a. Use sparse matrices to represent autocorrelation constraints\n   b. For each length $n$ in [128,256]:\n        - Extract subsequence centered from parent\n        - Start from initialized samples\n   c. Run two optimization phases: LP hunter and gradient scout\n\n3. **LP Hunter Phase:**\n   - Formulate and solve LP maximizing dual sum subject to autocorrelation bounds\n   - Use a sparse matrix representation of constraints\n   - Lower bound updates based on goodness of dual solutions\n\n4. **Gradient Scout Phase:**\n   - Use finite differences to compute gradient\n   - Perform line-search direction exploration\n   - Mix sequences preserving the good properties\n\n5. **Candidate Acceptance:**\n   - Verify solution via direct evaluation\n   - Resort candidates based on LC1 lower-better scoring\n\n6. **Termination:**\n   - Break upon stabilization\n   - Return best candidate found\n   - Ensure final sequence passes evaluator checks\n\nSearch Choices and Useful Variations\n- **Initializations**:\n  - Dirichlet (alpha=1.7) for smoothness diversity\n  - Normal perturbations of good seeds\n  - Half-wave sinusoidal patterns\n\n- **Optimization Parameters**:\n  - LP iterations: 50 at n=96, ret 30 at 128/256\n  - Mixing parameters: 0.3 initial, adaptive between 0.3-0.7\n  - Tim badging: Progressive reduction with iteration count\n\n- **Dimension Transitions**:\n  - Expansion: 50% window, linear extrapolation from parent\n  - Contraction: Even sampling from best parts\n\n- **Criteria Monitoring**:\n  - Early exit if similar solutions repeat\n  - Timeout penatelities applied to stagnation\n  - AC1 improvement rate as primary metric\n\nCompute Budget and Robustness\n- **Estimation**:\n  - 96-length: ~8e6 total operations\n  - 128: ~16e6, 256: ~32e6\n  - Wall time: 40sec/128, 60sec/256\n\n- **Job Scheduling**:\n  - Break tasks by sequence length\n  - Time checks inside LP and gradient calls\n  - Maintain soft failover for LP failures/NaN constraints\n\n- **Failover Management**:\n  - Time-based kills with best candidate retained\n  - Bootstrapping fallbacks for outlier values\n  - Normalization to prevent catastrophic deviation\n\nValidation and Return Contract\n- **Evaluation Precedence**:\n  - 7-out-of-8 candidates evaluated with evaluator\n  - Final candidate re-checked with exact_formula\n  - Score -inf rejected, +inf implies invalid\n\n- **Output Requirements**:\n  - Nonnegative real coefficients\n  - All below 1000.0\n  - List delimiter: comma-separated space\n\n- **SanityChecks**:\n  - Simulate periodic patterns and bound increases\n  - Validate time-distance mappings for loosely coupled steps\n  - Automatic fallback detection for outlying values",
